1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:03,247
A polygon is the next idea in geometry. It

2
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:06,120
is a simple closed figure made from a definite

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:09,980
number of straight line segments. Inside every polygon we

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,211
find sides, vertices, and diagonals. Let us learn their names.

5
00:00:13,707 --> 00:00:16,787
We already know a simple closed curve. But a

6
00:00:16,787 --> 00:00:18,620
smooth curve like this is not a polygon. When

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:22,667
its boundary becomes straight line segments, the figure is

8
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:24,138
called a polygon.

9
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:28,100
What must a polygon have? It must be made

10
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,434
of line segments, it must be closed, and it

11
00:00:31,434 --> 00:00:35,610
must not cross itself. Here are three segments, open,

12
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:38,483
so it is not a polygon yet. Join the

13
00:00:38,483 --> 00:00:41,327
ends and it closes into a triangle. Three sides

14
00:00:41,327 --> 00:00:43,631
is the smallest number that can close.

15
00:00:44,267 --> 00:00:47,564
Look at triangle ABC. Its three line segments are

16
00:00:47,564 --> 00:00:51,003
its sides. Its three corner points, A, B and

17
00:00:51,003 --> 00:00:54,824
C, are its vertices. Each vertex is the place

18
00:00:54,824 --> 00:00:56,298
where two sides meet.

19
00:00:56,913 --> 00:01:01,469
Now add a fourth vertex and build quadrilateral ABCD.

20
00:01:01,469 --> 00:01:04,313
Its four sides are AB, BC, CD, and DA.

21
00:01:04,313 --> 00:01:09,004
It has four vertices: A, B, C and D.

22
00:01:09,687 --> 00:01:12,707
Some parts are next to each other. Side AB

23
00:01:12,707 --> 00:01:17,067
shares vertex B with side BC, and shares vertex

24
00:01:17,067 --> 00:01:19,719
A with side DA. So AB is adjacent to

25
00:01:19,719 --> 00:01:24,187
BC, and adjacent to DA. Adjacent means next to,

26
00:01:24,187 --> 00:01:25,218
sharing a corner.

27
00:01:25,807 --> 00:01:30,607
Now look across the quadrilateral. Side CD does not

28
00:01:30,607 --> 00:01:33,607
touch side AB, so CD is the side opposite

29
00:01:33,607 --> 00:01:38,647
AB. Vertex A and vertex C are opposite vertices,

30
00:01:38,647 --> 00:01:40,338
and so are B and D.

31
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:44,300
Join the opposite vertices. The segment from A to

32
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:47,340
C is a diagonal. The segment from B to

33
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:52,600
D is the second diagonal. So quadrilateral ABCD has

34
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,111
two diagonals: AC and BD.

35
00:01:55,807 --> 00:01:58,887
Do not mix up a side and a diagonal.

36
00:01:58,887 --> 00:02:02,335
A side is part of the boundary, like AB.

37
00:02:02,335 --> 00:02:07,479
A diagonal joins opposite vertices across the inside, like

38
00:02:07,479 --> 00:02:11,718
AC. BC and DA are sides, while BD is a diagonal.

39
00:02:12,327 --> 00:02:15,427
Your turn. Four quick checks on quadrilateral PQRS. First,

40
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:19,347
name the four sides. Second, name the sides adjacent

41
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:23,787
to PQ. Third, name the two diagonals. And last

42
00:02:23,787 --> 00:02:26,718
of all: is this open chain a polygon?

43
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:41,680
The four sides are PQ, QR, RS, and SP.

44
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:45,633
The sides adjacent to PQ are QR and PS,

45
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:50,315
because they share an endpoint with PQ. The diagonals

46
00:02:50,315 --> 00:02:53,223
are PR and QS. And no, the open chain

47
00:02:53,223 --> 00:02:57,071
is not a polygon, because it is not closed.

48
00:02:57,713 --> 00:03:00,685
One last look. A polygon is a simple closed

49
00:03:00,685 --> 00:03:04,533
figure made of line segments. Its boundary segments are

50
00:03:04,533 --> 00:03:07,397
its sides, and its corner points are its vertices.

51
00:03:07,397 --> 00:03:11,269
Sides that share a vertex are adjacent. And line

52
00:03:11,269 --> 00:03:15,533
segments that join opposite vertices are diagonals. Know the

53
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:18,418
parts, and you understand the polygon. Thank you for

54
00:03:18,418 --> 00:03:20,884
watching, and see you in the next lesson.
